Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0008 + 0010 + 0011.
DSpark greedy drafts argmaxed per vocabulary shard (VLLM_DSPARK_LOCAL_ARGMAX=1, with VLLM_DSPARK_MARKOV_CACHE). The
sequential Markov sampling all-gathered the full draft logits from the TP-sharded lm_head (129,280 columns a draft row)
and added a full-vocab Markov bias on every rank at every draft position. Now each rank adds the bias for its own
columns only (the Markov cache built over its row range of the replicated markov_w2: half the rows and half the cache
memory at TP=2) to its own shard of the base logits, takes the local max, and all-gathers one (value, index) pair per
row, the reduction vLLM's LogitsProcessor.get_top_tokens uses for vocab-parallel argmax. Equal maxima resolve to the
lower rank, i.e. the lower vocabulary index, so the drafts are the tokens the full path picks, bit for bit (same base
logit columns, same bias kernel per column). Greedy drafting only, and only without the acceptance estimator (it reads
full logits; the confidence head replaces it under the depth policy). TensorFold's V4.1 drafter splits its Markov dot
by vocabulary halves with a (value, index) argmax gather the same way (github.com/bertholomus/TensorFold, branch
deepseek-v41-tp2, families/deepseek_v41/cuda/markov.py, Apache-2.0); this is our implementation for vLLM.
Test: patches/tests/test_dspark_local_argmax.py.

